Let

\[
f(w)=2^{\operatorname{inv}(w)},\qquad w\in S_6.
\]

Then \(A_{\sigma,\tau}=f(\sigma^{-1}\tau)\) is the Varchenko matrix of the braid arrangement \(x_i=x_j\), with every hyperplane assigned weight \(2\). For the braid arrangement of type \(A_{n-1}\), the determinant is

\[
\det\bigl(q^{\operatorname{inv}(\sigma^{-1}\tau)}\bigr)_{\sigma,\tau\in S_n}
=
\prod_{k=2}^{n}
\left(1-q^{k(k-1)}\right)^{
\frac{n!(n-k+1)}{k(k-1)}
}.
\]

Here the factor \(1-q^{k(k-1)}\) comes from a block of \(k\) coordinates becoming equal: there are \(\binom nk\) such blocks, each contributing exponent \((k-2)!(n-k+1)!\), and

\[
\binom nk (k-2)!(n-k+1)!
=
\frac{n!(n-k+1)}{k(k-1)}.
\]

For \(n=6\), the exponents are

\[
\begin{aligned}
k=2 &: \frac{720\cdot 5}{2}=1800,\\
k=3 &: \frac{720\cdot 4}{6}=480,\\
k=4 &: \frac{720\cdot 3}{12}=180,\\
k=5 &: \frac{720\cdot 2}{20}=72,\\
k=6 &: \frac{720\cdot 1}{30}=24.
\end{aligned}
\]

Substituting \(q=2\),

\[
\det A
=
(1-2^2)^{1800}
(1-2^6)^{480}
(1-2^{12})^{180}
(1-2^{20})^{72}
(1-2^{30})^{24}.
\]

The total exponent \(1800+480+180+72+24=2556\) is even, so the determinant is positive. Therefore

\[
\boxed{
3^{1800}\,63^{480}\,4095^{180}\,1048575^{72}\,1073741823^{24}
}
\]
